course: dictionary
lesson: 35
title: Academic: school words and what they mean
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Academic is a word about school and learning. It is most often used for reading, writing and maths, the subjects you study in a classroom. «She is not the most academic, but she is a brilliant painter.» Here academic means not very good at school work, and the rest of the sentence tells you she is good at something else.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Academic can also name a person: an academic is someone who teaches or does research at a university. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning is being used. A professor at a university is an academic, but a child in your class is not.
explain: «More practical than academic» is a kind way to describe someone. A boy who is more practical than academic finds school work hard, but he is good at making and doing things with his hands. The clues are the words "practical" and "hands", so the sentence is kind, not cruel.
fact: Academic means to do with school, study and learning.
fact: Academic work is mostly reading, writing and maths, not practical skills.
fact: An academic is a person who teaches or does research at a university.
fact: «Not the most academic» means not clever at school work, said politely.
fact: «It's academic» means something no longer matters, because it will not change anything.
exercise: «She is not the most academic, but she is a brilliant painter.» What does academic mean here? | Always late for school | *Not very good at school work | Very good at painting | Lost in the classroom
exercise: A teacher says, «He is more practical than academic.» What does this suggest? | He is the top student in every subject | He never goes to school | *He finds school work hard but is good with his hands | He only likes reading books
exercise: «The academic year starts in September.» What does academic mean here? | *To do with school and learning | To do with sport and running | To do with the sea and boats | To do with cooking food
test: «Whether we win the game now is academic; the match is already over.» What does academic mean here? | *It no longer matters | It is a university teacher | It is very clever | It is about school
test: Dr Patel is an academic at the university. What is she? | A builder of houses | A person who never reads | *A teacher or researcher at a university | A pupil in a primary school
exam: Which word means to do with school, study and learning, especially reading, writing and maths? | glum | practical | *academic | barely
